    "description": "Closes #1510
### Root Cause
With `formalGithubReview: true`, `postGeneralComment` and `formalApproveBody`/`formalRejectBody` both resolved the same `reviewData.generalComment` through `resolveGeneralCommentText` with no per-target formatting — the formal review posted a byte-identical copy of the general comment (case 1 of the ticket's divergence matrix). Two adjacent defects shared the block: a falsy `generalComment` field skipped the comment but not the full-text review (cases 2–3 asymmetry, including a "See PR comments" stub on reviews with no comments), and the own-PR 422 rejection warned with a hedged `own-PR restriction?` naming no identities.

### Fix
- `js/common/formalReviewCard.js` (new, pure): compact verdict-card builders — `## Automated Code Review — <verdict>`, a `blocking N · important N · suggestions N · digest N` census line, and a `Full review:` pointer that is only ever honest (comment URL when the provider returned one; "see the review summary comment above" only when the comment actually posted; no pointer when nothing was posted), plus the own-PR rejection warning naming PR author + configured reviewer logins.
- `js/postPRReviewComments.js`: single general-comment resolution hoisted in `postGitHubReview`; `postGeneralCommentText` posts the resolved text and returns `{ posted, url }` (from the `github_add_pr_comment` return, defensively unwrapped); the formal review consumes that result. Extracted into the new module to respect the module-size ratchet (file shrank 3422→3382 lines; pin lowered and locked).
- Untouched per ticket: verdict record, `pr_approved` label, `dismissPriorChangeRequests`, opt-out semantics, SCM-without-`submitReview` path.

### Test Coverage
- `js/unit-tests/test_postPRReviewComments.js`: 5 new/rewritten e2e formal-review cases (APPROVE card ≠ general text with census + pointer; case 2 field-absent/file-present; case 3 nothing-resolvable bare card; inline markdown unchanged; REQUEST_CHANGES conditional stub) + the own-PR 422 honest-warn case — all RED before the fix, GREEN after (218 passed).
- `js/unit-tests/test_formalReviewCard.js` (new, 9 cases) wired into `run_all.json`.
- Full suite: 10968 passed; the 16 failures are byte-identical to the base commit `8b545df` (verified via a clean worktree run) — pre-existing, unrelated.
- Quality gates replicated locally: module-size ratchet, nesting, CRAP ≤ 8 + coverage (exit 0), duplication ratchet (exit 0), crap4dart similarity (clean for tracked files), pack require gate (exit 0).

### Notes
- Behavior change by design: with the flag on, the formal review no longer carries the full review text (the comment keeps it) — consumers keying on full text in the review body should read the comment or the census card.
- The own-PR warn names the PR author and the configured machine-author logins (`machineAuthor` knob); the token's live login is not resolvable with the existing tool set, so the configured identity is reported."
